get.description:
**Roles:** clinician, physician

Upgrade to a WebSocket at `wss://<host>/api/v1/ws/stream`. Browsers cannot set an Authorization header on a WebSocket, so the client first calls `POST /auth/ws-ticket` and passes the single-use ticket as `?ticket=`. The server pushes only events for the caller's care team patients.

Server messages:
```json
{"type": "vital", "patient_id": "00000000-0000-4000-b000-000000000005", "data": {"recorded_at": "2026-10-21T09:48:00-06:00", "context": "exercise", "heart_rate": 138, "quality": "valid"}}
{"type": "alert", "data": {"alert_id": "00000000-0000-4000-f000-000000000001", "patient_id": "00000000-0000-4000-b000-000000000005", "severity": "critical", "rule_code": "HR_ABOVE_CEILING", "title": "Heart rate 138 bpm above ceiling of 128 bpm", "triggered_at": "2026-10-21T09:48:20-06:00", "triggering_values": {"heart_rate": [133, 138], "ceiling": 128}, "link": "https://app.healthtrack.example/alerts/00000000-0000-4000-f000-000000000001"}}
{"type": "alert_status", "data": {"alert_id": "00000000-0000-4000-f000-000000000001", "status": "acknowledged", "by": "00000000-0000-4000-a000-000000000002"}}
{"type": "heartbeat", "ts": "2026-10-21T09:48:30-06:00"}
```
Client messages: `{"type": "subscribe", "patient_ids": [...]}` narrows the stream; ids outside scope are ignored.
